# Implementation Plan: Resolve Merge Conflicts & Merge Branches

This plan details the steps to resolve merge conflicts arising from merging the `lou` branch into the `develop` branch (which already contains the merged `jeff` branch changes). It also addresses a critical runtime bug identified in the user profile updates.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Duplicate Supabase Migration Conflict**: Both the `jeff` and `lou` branches migrated `syntaxure-labs` from Firebase to Supabase independently. This has introduced multiple conflicts in user profile handling, login redirects, project management views, and audit logging.
> 
> **Critical User Profile Database Bug**: We identified that `apps/syntaxure-labs/src/app/actions/users.ts`'s `updateUserProfile` function currently sends raw `UserProfile` fields (e.g. `displayName`, `photoURL`, `title`, `location`) directly to PostgreSQL. However, these are not columns in the `user_profiles` table (the columns are `full_name`, `avatar_url`, and the generic `preferences` JSONB column). Running this update will trigger a runtime SQL error. We have included a robust fix for this as part of this merge.

## Proposed Changes

Here is the strategy to resolve the conflicts in each file:

### Build System & Configuration

---

#### [MODIFY] [turbo.json](file:///c:/dev/Next%20Js/jeffdev-monorepo/turbo.json)
- **Conflict**: Duplicate `ANALYZE` and trailing comma placement for `USE_GREMLIN_RANKING` under `globalEnv`.
- **Resolution**: Keep `USE_GREMLIN_RANKING` as the last environment variable without a trailing comma, and ensure `ANALYZE` is listed only once.

---

### Shared Application Views

#### [MODIFY] [calendar/page.tsx](file:///c:/dev/Next%20Js/jeffdev-monorepo/apps/prism-manage/src/app/(dashboard)/calendar/page.tsx)
- **Conflict**: Import and usage of `useProjects()` added in the `lou` branch.
- **Resolution**: Keep the `useProjects()` import and hook execution from the `lou` branch to ensure proper project context mapping in the calendar dashboard.

---

### Syntaxure Labs Application

#### [MODIFY] [calendar.ts](file:///c:/dev/Next%20Js/jeffdev-monorepo/apps/syntaxure-labs/src/app/actions/calendar.ts)
- **Conflict**: Trivial whitespace differences.
- **Resolution**: Clean up the conflict markers and keep the clean workspace.

#### [MODIFY] [login/page.tsx](file:///c:/dev/Next%20Js/jeffdev-monorepo/apps/syntaxure-labs/src/app/admin/login/page.tsx)
- **Conflict**: OAuth redirect URI points to `/auth/callback` in HEAD (`jeff`) versus `/api/auth/callback` in `lou`.
- **Resolution**: Keep the redirect URI pointing to `/auth/callback` (HEAD), as `/auth/callback/route.ts` is the actual callback route implemented in the application. Drop the unused `useRouter` import from `lou`.

#### [MODIFY] [profile/page.tsx](file:///c:/dev/Next%20Js/jeffdev-monorepo/apps/syntaxure-labs/src/app/admin/profile/page.tsx)
- **Conflict**: Duplicate imports and differences in user profile schema mapping from PostgreSQL.
- **Resolution**: Map extra metadata fields (such as `title`, `location`, `status`, and `assignedProjects`) from the `preferences` JSONB column instead of trying to read them directly from database columns where they do not exist. Use `getAdminClient` to fetch the profile to ensure proper server-side authentication validation.

#### [MODIFY] [users.ts](file:///c:/dev/Next%20Js/jeffdev-monorepo/apps/syntaxure-labs/src/app/actions/users.ts) *(Pre-emptive bugfix)*
- **Issue**: Attempting to update `displayName`, `photoURL`, `location`, etc., as direct table columns will crash in PostgreSQL.
- **Resolution**: Intercept updates in `updateUserProfile`. Map `displayName` -> `full_name`, `photoURL` -> `avatar_url`. Merge `title`, `location`, `status`, `assignedProjects`, `social`, and `namecard` into the `preferences` JSONB object, then execute a safe update.

#### [MODIFY] [projects/[slug]/page.tsx](file:///c:/dev/Next%20Js/jeffdev-monorepo/apps/syntaxure-labs/src/app/admin/projects/[slug]/page.tsx)
- **Conflict**: Path references for types (`types/firestore` in HEAD vs `types/supabase` in `lou`).
- **Resolution**: Use the renamed `types/supabase` import for `FirestoreProject` and `ProjectMilestone`, and retain the `DeleteProjectButton` import from HEAD.

#### [MODIFY] [audit.ts](file:///c:/dev/Next%20Js/jeffdev-monorepo/apps/syntaxure-labs/src/lib/audit.ts)
- **Conflict**: Trivial whitespace differences.
- **Resolution**: Clean up conflict markers and retain the existing file content.

#### [MODIFY] [feature-flags.ts](file:///c:/dev/Next%20Js/jeffdev-monorepo/apps/syntaxure-labs/src/lib/feature-flags.ts)
- **Conflict**: Handling of unused `flags` parameter in `updateFeatureFlags`.
- **Resolution**: Keep HEAD's `console.log(...)` expression which correctly uses the `flags` parameter, avoiding a `Cannot find name '_flags'` TypeScript error present in the `lou` branch version.

